Across the vast reaches of the sea,
partly covered by the ocean floor,
rest the bound remains of the dead,
their arms and legs still locked in irons.

Farther down than the dew ever settles,
sunk lower than any weighted line can reach,
drift vessels carrying their entire crews,
never again to descend or rise upward.

Down there glides the dark vessel of bondage,
loaded with its cargo of human beings,
whose chained and decayed bones
lie beyond the reach of any tempest.

These remains belong to the enslaved;
they shine out from the deep waters below;
from the gaping ocean they call out,
"We stand as living proof of these crimes!"

Throughout the broad expanse of the land,
places exist where human beings are sold;
their throats are worn raw by iron collars,
their hands squeezed tight by binding cuffs.

Corpses left for the birds of prey
to feed upon in barren wastelands;
killings so horrifying that they
drive children in terror from their games!

Every wicked notion and wrongful act;
rage, unchecked desire, and arrogance;
the most vile and overgrown of weeds
that smother the suffering current of Life!

These are the sorrows of the enslaved;
they stare out fiercely from the depths;
from graves unmarked and hidden they call,
"We stand as living proof of these crimes!"
